though it shows (packages/escher-driver/src/lib.rs:72-78) — and, since 2026-10-10-snapshot-states, in one sentence that an element stating itself selected, pressed or invalid in its markup reads so as true or false, with the two limits — a mixed toggle reads not pressed, a grammar or spelling error reads invalid (packages/escher-driver/src/lib.rs:68-72) — since 2026-10-12-self-description the sentence says each limit is stated in its node key's help, where the table states it, and that a changed node names the keys whose reading differs (`differs`); the driver's logic is unchanged and no file of the driver states either fixed limit. The `covered` reading as it now stands, in both layout modes: a control lying where a scrolling box's scrolled-out row extends, before the box in the document or after it, is hit and clicked as itself — its handler runs and no row's, and since 2026-10-13-stand-keyboard-harness the clicked button reads `focused` after the accepted click, a click focusing a button in every document ([Scrolling and input]) — because the engine's hit stops at the padding box of a box paint clips (the Scrolling, selection, tree contract above); two readings are off — a box with no width or no height, hit at its centre on the element that holds it, which reads `covered` though nothing covers it (the stand's `task-header-spacer`, 0 high; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_ids.rs:60), and a target lying beside a box clipped on one axis, along the axis it does not clip, which reads in view and is refused `covered` with the instance unchanged, in both layout modes (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_obstructed.rs:560-605; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep/report.md); `stand_act_obstructed` holds both readings (as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-scrolling-box-bounds-and-hit/report.md; the reading it replaces at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-driver-cli/evidence/engine-findings.md). `Command`, `Call` and `ArgValue` derive